WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.350
CARTER MORGAN: Creating
a safe work environment

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.860
is more important than ever.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:03.990
Not only can it
help protect workers

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:06.032
from injury and illness,
but it can raise morale,

00:00:06.032 --> 00:00:08.100
reduce absenteeism and
turnover, and improve

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.445
overall productivity.

00:00:09.445 --> 00:00:11.070
However, creating a
working environment

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.380
where employees both
are safe and feel safe

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.580
can be challenging.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.250
For instance, proper safety
protocols and procedures

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.590
have to be clear, accessible,
and easy for everyone

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.910
to follow.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.230
Appropriate feedback
channels must be in place

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.230
so safety concerns can
be reported and addressed

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.670
in a short amount of time.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.350
Safety documentation
and procedures

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.200
have to be meticulously
tracked, stored, and protected.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.110
This can be a huge undertaking,
but luckily, Google Cloud

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.250
is here to help.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.200
By leveraging Google
Cloud technology,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.700
organizations can
create a workplace

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.812
that is more productive,
safer, and happier.

00:00:40.812 --> 00:00:42.270
Let's see how an
organization could

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.312
use these products to
better identify and address

00:00:44.312 --> 00:00:45.930
their safety issues.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:46.800
Meet Ashley.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.140
Ashley leads the safety team
at a growing manufacturing

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:49.912
company.

00:00:49.912 --> 00:00:51.870
Although they don't have
any coding experience,

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:53.537
Ashley and her team
have created a suite

00:00:53.537 --> 00:00:56.130
of safety apps using AppSheet,
Google Cloud's no-code app

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.505
development platform.

00:00:57.505 --> 00:00:59.130
Each of their employees
and contractors

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:01.088
are able to download
these apps and access them

00:01:01.088 --> 00:01:03.070
at any time on their
mobile devices.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:05.519
One day Han, who works in
the manufacturing facility,

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:07.680
slips and almost falls
while walking up the stairs

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:08.915
outside their building.

00:01:08.915 --> 00:01:10.290
Instead of ignoring
the incident,

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.748
Han knows that
there is an easy way

00:01:11.748 --> 00:01:13.740
to report any risk he notices.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.960
He's able to open up his
safety risk reporting app

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.220
and fill out a form
detailing the safety risk,

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:30.090
including the risk
level, details, picture,

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.170
and even annotations.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.090
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:34.920
Once he completes
the form, Ashley,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.690
who is on the safety
board, is immediately

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:38.580
notified of the issue.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.865
She's able to open the report,
read through the details,

00:01:41.865 --> 00:01:42.740
and claim the ticket.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.550
Ashley wants to understand
the situation better,

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.000
so she sets up a
meeting to talk to Han.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.510
They join a Google
Meet video call

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.972
so they can talk face to face.

00:01:53.972 --> 00:01:56.180
Her team decides they would
like to hire a contractor

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.898
to install railings along
both sides of the stairs.

00:01:58.898 --> 00:02:00.440
They work with the
management, legal,

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.870
and finance teams in real
time to update and finalize

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:05.020
the contract.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.850
Back in the app, Ashley is able
to document the steps taken

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:08.780
to address this risk.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:12.119
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.430
Once the contractor is finished
installing the railings,

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:18.630
Ashley is able to close the
ticket by selecting Resolve.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.360
This is just one example of
the many types of safety apps

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.040
you could build.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.540
Using these Google
Cloud solutions,

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.998
creating applications
such as these

00:02:25.998 --> 00:02:28.020
can take days or weeks,
not months or years

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:32.270
to build, allowing businesses to
work safer, faster, and better.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:35.130
To learn more and to access
this and other app templates,

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:36.300
click on the link below.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.650
